namespace pdg { /**
\fn pdg::SpriteLayer::removeSprite(Sprite oldSprite)
\brief Remove a Sprite and its mounted descendants from this layer.

Preserves mount relationships and layer-coordinate transforms. Retained groups can be animated off-layer and added to another layer. Removing a mounted child independently throws; detach it first. Sprites outside this layer are unchanged. Physics bodies leave the shared solver and retain their state for basic integration; root constraints and physical animation rigs are disconnected.

\param oldSprite The root of the group to remove.

\note Native callers must retain the host with addRef()/release() to keep it alive after removal. JavaScript handles retain automatically. Removal from a locked physics callback is deferred until the solve ends. Animation modifiers cannot change layer membership.
\see addSprite(), Part::detachSprite(), removeAllSprites()
**/ }
